":"Leading post-Minkowskian correction.","filename":"tail1.png"},{"key":"0507313411b8f1338b7bde561078bf63","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/0507313411b8f1338b7bde561078bf63","source":"arxiv","caption":"Second order post-Minkowskian corrections.","filename":"tail2.png"},{"key":"4dcf3ada4aa2ea607d27070f33fa21f5","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/4dcf3ada4aa2ea607d27070f33fa21f5","source":"arxiv","caption":"The series of leading IR poles.","filename":"ladders.png"},{"key":"aac5996b439d52555551b082cf98648c","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/aac5996b439d52555551b082cf98648c","source":"arxiv","caption":"Feynman diagram yielding the leading terms for $T^{00}$ and $T^{0i}$.","filename":"t00+0ilo.png"},{"key":"a97d3ca9a524df9b0f79058f81e7863e","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a97d3ca9a524df9b0f79058f81e7863e","source":"arxiv","caption":"Diagrams for $v^2$ corrections to $T^{00}$. Dashed lines denote potential gravitons.","filename":"t00nlo.png"},{"key":"9c9c45de01eaefd0beef264ddb92633c","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/9c9c45de01eaefd0beef264ddb92633c","source":"arxiv","caption":"Diagrams needed to compute the leading contribution to $T^{ij}$.","filename":"tijlo.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["Goldberger:2009qd"],"citeable":true,"keywords":[{"value":"11.27.+d","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"04.25.Nx","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"04.30.Db","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"11.10.Gh","schema":"PACS"},{"value":"expansion: multipole","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"moment: monopole","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"energy: flux","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"effective field theory","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"gravitational radiation","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"renormalization","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"higher-order: 0","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"energy: correction","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"singularity: infrared","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"singularity: ultraviolet","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"In this paper we construct an effective field theory (EFT) that describes long wavelength gravitational radiation from compact systems. To leading order, this EFT consists of the multipole expansion, which we describe in terms of a diffeomorphism invariant point particle Lagrangian. The EFT also systematically captures \"post-Minkowskian\" corrections to the multipole expansion due to non-linear terms in general relativity. Specifically, we compute long distance corrections from the coupling of the (mass) monopole moment to the quadrupole moment, including up to two mass insertions. Along the way, we encounter both logarithmic short distance (UV) and long wavelength (IR) divergences. We show that the UV divergences can be (1) absorbed into a renormalization of the multipole moments and (2) resummed via the renormalization group. The IR singularities are shown to cancel from properly defined physical observables. As a concrete example of the formalism, we use this EFT to reproduce a number of post-Newtonian corrections to the gravitational wave energy flux from non-relativistic binaries, including long distance effects up to 3PN ($v^6$) order. Our results verify that the factorization of scales proposed in the NRGR framework of Goldberger and Rothstein is consistent up to order 3PN.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/348147"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"325","page_start":"325","journal_title":"Science","journal_volume":"256"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/272672"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"518","page_start":"518","journal_title":"Nucl.Instrum.Meth.A","journal_volume":"289"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/619185"},"reference":{"publication_info":{"artid":"S1","page_start":"S1","journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav.","journal_volume":"20"}},"cur